KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[handler\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ terminate called from the unwinding: SUCCESS$
^\[handler\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Soundness: remove_cpp_exceptions (instrument_unwind_call) assumes that a
destructor called during stack unwinding does not exit via an exception,
so the path on which std::terminate runs the handler is removed: both
assertions of the handler hold.  The exit has to call std::terminate,
which calls the handler installed by std::set_terminate; std::set_terminate
and std::terminate also have no body (libsupc++, libc++abi).
